    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "# Issue\r\nI may be mis-interpreting what this example function is supposed to do. I thought this was supposed to open the selected file from the explorer buffer as a split (vert of horizontal). However, in practice all this appears to do is duplicate the existing active buffer.\r\n\r\nI have modified the code as such to get the intended result of opening the selected file as a split:\r\n```lua\r\n\t-- Open buffers in split\r\n\tlocal map_split = function(buf_id, lhs, direction)\r\n\t    local rhs = function()\r\n\t\t-- Make new window and set it as target\r\n\t\tlocal cur_target = MiniFiles.get_explorer_state().target_window\r\n\t\tlocal new_target = vim.api.nvim_win_call(cur_target, function()\r\n\t\t    vim.cmd(direction .. ' split')\r\n\t\t    return vim.api.nvim_get_current_win()\r\n\t\tend)\r\n\r\n\t\tMiniFiles.set_target_window(new_target)\r\n-----------MY ADDITION START\r\n\t\t-- Get the file path of the selected item\r\n\t\tlocal file_path = MiniFiles.get_fs_entry().path\r\n\r\n\t\t-- Open the file in the new split if a file is selected\r\n\t\tif file_path then\r\n\t\t    vim.api.nvim_win_set_buf(new_target, vim.fn.bufadd(file_path))\r\n\t\telse\r\n\t\t    vim.notify(\"No file selected\", vim.log.levels.WARN)\r\n\t\tend\r\n----------MY ADDITION END\r\n\t    end\r\n\r\n\t    -- Adding `desc` will result into `show_help` entries\r\n\t    local desc = 'Split ' .. direction\r\n\t    vim.keymap.set('n', lhs, rhs, { buffer = buf_id, desc = desc })\r\n\tend\r\n\r\n\tvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', {\r\n\t    pattern = 'MiniFilesBufferCreate',\r\n\t    callback = function(args)\r\n\t\tlocal buf_id = args.data.buf_id\r\n\t\t-- Tweak keys to your liking\r\n\t\tmap_split(buf_id, '<C-s>', 'belowright horizontal')\r\n\t\tmap_split(buf_id, '<C-v>', 'belowright vertical')\r\n\t    end,\r\n\t})\r\n```\r\n\r\n# Doc Reference\r\nhttps://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/733afb94ed88d32b839a644dc137604691e46032/lua/mini/files.lua#L468C1-L497C9",
