            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "It works *exactly* as the title says: [\"Create mappings to **modify target window via split**\"](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/733afb94ed88d32b839a644dc137604691e46032/lua/mini/files.lua#L468). This means that it creates the split expecting user to follow up with either `l` (\"go in\") or `L` (\"go in and close the explorer\").\r\n\r\nIf you want to automatically go in, replace all the custom code with appropriate usage of [`go_in()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/733afb94ed88d32b839a644dc137604691e46032/doc/mini-files.txt#L770).",
